 EOF
 
+# NOTE: Earlier sessions added a 55-marathon-hw.conf with
+#   console=tty0 / splash / plymouth.use-simpledrm
+# on the theory that tty1 wasn't routed to the HyperPixel framebuffer.
+# That theory was WRONG. On the HackberryPi CM5 with HyperPixel
+# 4 Square, console=tty1 from 50-device-raspberry-pi5.conf DOES route
+# to the panel — what was hiding the boot was plymouth taking over the
+# framebuffer via simpledrm before the kernel's vc4-kms-dpi-hyperpixel4sq
+# DRM driver was ready. Result: dark screen for the entire boot window
+# (and the "device isn't booting" diagnosis was a mirage —
+# see [[duranium-pi5-boot-recipe]] for the post-mortem).
+#
+# Do not reintroduce this file without testing on real CM5 hardware.
+# (Removing only — no replacement written.)
+
+# Bake the Pimoroni HyperPixel 4.0 Square overlay into the Pi 5 base DTB.
+# postmarketOS' linux-postmarketos-stable kernel ships bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb
+# but NONE of the rpi-firmware userland overlays (vc4-kms-dpi-hyperpixel4sq.dtbo
+# etc.) — those live in upstream raspberrypi/firmware, which the pmOS aports
+# don't include. Without the overlay applied, the kernel has no DPI panel
+# node, /dev/fb0 never materialises on HyperPixel hardware, and
+# console=tty0 emits to a non-existent framebuffer = blank screen.
+#
+# The dtbo is vendored at marathon-extras/dtbos/vc4-kms-dpi-hyperpixel4sq.dtbo
+# (from raspberrypi/firmware:master). We use fdtoverlay to merge it into the
+# kernel-installed bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb in-place so mkosi's Devicetrees=*
+# picks up the merged DTB unmodified. Pi 5 UEFI boot passes this merged DTB
+# to the kernel via the EFI DTB Configuration Table.
+DTBO="$BUILDROOT/usr/share/marathon-dtbos/vc4-kms-dpi-hyperpixel4sq.dtbo"
+PI5_DTB="$BUILDROOT/boot/dtbs/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb"
+if [ -f "$PI5_DTB" ] && [ -f "$DTBO" ]; then
+    cp "$PI5_DTB" "$PI5_DTB.orig"
+    fdtoverlay -i "$PI5_DTB.orig" -o "$PI5_DTB" "$DTBO" 2>&1 || {
+        echo "WARN: fdtoverlay failed for HyperPixel — restoring upstream DTB" >&2
+        mv "$PI5_DTB.orig" "$PI5_DTB"
+    }
+    [ -f "$PI5_DTB.orig" ] && rm -f "$PI5_DTB.orig"
+fi
+# Same for the D-stepping Pi 5 silicon variant — both share carrier pinout.
+PI5D_DTB="$BUILDROOT/boot/dtbs/broadcom/bcm2712-d-rpi-5-b.dtb"
+if [ -f "$PI5D_DTB" ] && [ -f "$DTBO" ]; then
+    cp "$PI5D_DTB" "$PI5D_DTB.orig"
+    fdtoverlay -i "$PI5D_DTB.orig" -o "$PI5D_DTB" "$DTBO" 2>&1 || {
+        echo "WARN: fdtoverlay failed for HyperPixel (D-step) — restoring" >&2
+        mv "$PI5D_DTB.orig" "$PI5D_DTB"
+    }
+    [ -f "$PI5D_DTB.orig" ] && rm -f "$PI5D_DTB.orig"
+fi
+
 # Belt-and-suspenders for the QSettings pre-seed: a one-shot systemd unit that
 # runs as 'user' BEFORE greetd starts marathon-shell, copies the factory file
 # in place, and marks itself complete. tmpfiles.d 'C+' alone isn't reliable
